 docker run --env BASE_URL=https://fizzy.example.com ...
 ```
 
+#### Push notifications (optional)
+
+Fizzy can send web push notifications to people's phones and desktops whenever something lands in their tray.
+To enable them, generate a VAPID key pair:
+
+```sh
+docker run --rm ghcr.io/basecamp/fizzy:latest bin/rails runner 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{key.public_key}"; puts "VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{key.private_key}"'
+```
+
+Then hand both values to Fizzy as environment variables:
+
+- `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` - the public key, which the browser uses when subscribing
+- `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` - the private key, which Fizzy uses to sign push requests
+
+Once set, people can turn on notifications for each of their devices from their notification settings.
+
 #### S3 storage (optional)
 
 If you'd prefer that uploaded files were stored in an S3 bucket rather than in your mounted volume, you can set that up.
